{
 "_comment": [
  "FACTORtv — THE CAREER LADDERS.",
  "",
  "Six paths a driver can climb, each a list of TIERS in order. This is data",
  "rather than code because it is curated by the user: he owns the car mods,",
  "he knows which are raceable, and he is still adding to them.",
  "",
  "WHY THE CAR LIST IS HAND-KEPT AND NOT SCANNED. Installed does not mean",
  "raceable. The Studio 397 GT3 cars sit fully downloaded — 188MB apiece,",
  "same folder shape and same .mas files as free content — and will not load",
  "without the licence. Nothing on disk distinguishes them, so a scan would",
  "confidently offer a tier the user cannot race. The folder scan suggests;",
  "this file decides.",
  "",
  "TWO WAYS TO MATCH A CAR, because the two names are not the same thing:",
  "  `mods`    installed folder names. Known before a car has ever been",
  "            loaded, so the menu can draw the whole ladder from a cold",
  "            start. Matched on a normalised substring, like track.ALIASES.",
  "  `classes` the CarClass string rF2 reports in shared memory and in result",
  "            files. This is what a LIVE session gives us, and it is how a",
  "            race is credited to a rung. Present in every session type —",
  "            practice and qualifying included.",
  "",
  "`needs` is the championship position required IN THE TIER BELOW to earn a",
  "seat here. Null on an entry tier. The numbers escalate on purpose: fifth",
  "gets you out of karting, second gets you into Formula One. The bar rising",
  "as you climb is the whole shape of a racing career, and it explains itself",
  "without a tutorial.",
  "",
  "`register` picks how the booth SOUNDS at this tier — see booth_ladder.json.",
  "It is a tone, not a knowledge base: there is no real history to draw on in",
  "a karting field, and inventing some would be the one thing this product",
  "refuses to do."
 ],
